TODO items for mcstas-ess-instr-citool
======================================

* runci: Consider running the tests of the different modes in parallel (as
  independent mctest runs, each with its own test directory), to make CI
  faster for projects with several modes. MPI (runci --mpi) does not help
  much for typical tests, since compilation with MPI takes longer, and the
  default mctest simulations are short.

* runci: The JSON test results produced by mctest are only used to check for
  failures which mctest did not report in its exit code (see check_results
  in runtest.py). Decide whether to use them for anything else (e.g.
  summarise, store as CI artifacts, compare between runs).

* generatepy: The instrument renaming and the translation of %Example lines
  into McStasScript tests are done by the tool when mcstas-pygen does not
  support this (McStas 3.8.8). These features were added to mcstas-pygen in
  https://github.com/mccode-dev/McCode/pull/2707 (merged, not yet released).
  Once a McStas release with them is required, remove the workarounds in
  generatepy.py. Also, the generated test code works around McStasScript
  add_test issues fixed in
  https://github.com/PaNOSC-ViNYL/McStasScript/pull/138 (merged, not yet
  released), and could be simplified once that release is required.

* instrpy projects with includes/: The code generated by generatepy adds the
  package directory to the DEPENDENCY line with McStasScript's
  add_dependency, which is proposed in
  https://github.com/PaNOSC-ViNYL/McStasScript/pull/139, and falls back to
  set_dependency and the undocumented dependency_statement attribute
  otherwise. That PR also adds add_include_dir, which does exactly this
  (absolute path with forward slashes, no whitespace). Once it is merged,
  use add_include_dir when available, and once a McStasScript release with
  it is required, remove the fallback.

* %Example lines without any parameters fail in mctest (the instrument then
  asks for the parameter values interactively). An upstream fix for mctest
  has been proposed in https://github.com/mccode-dev/McCode/pull/2708 (which
  passes -y for such lines). Until a McStas release with this fix is
  required, such lines must list at least one parameter (as done by
  add_example in the ExPyHelpers example).

* localdata/: Consider a size limit (or a policy for large files, e.g. Git
  LFS) for data files. In the surveyed instrument repositories, the largest
  data file is a 38 MB .hkl file (MAGiC).

* mcstas-pygen drops SEARCH statements, so generatepy adds
  instr.add_search() for localcomps/ itself. Consider proposing upstream that
  mcstas-pygen translates SEARCH statements into instr.add_search() calls
  (relative paths would need care, since McStasScript runs the instrument
  elsewhere).

* NCrystal resolves relative paths of data files (e.g.
  "localdata/X.ncmat") only relative to the working directory, unlike McStas
  components using read_table-lib, which also look relative to the .instr
  file. Consider proposing upstream that the NCrystal McStas components also
  look relative to the .instr file, so instruments can also be run from other
  directories.
